<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 19.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 19.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period February 17-19.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Feb 17 (actual) 306 mcm, 72 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 18 (forecast) 310 mcm, 73 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 19 (forecast) 316 mcm, 74 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Feb 17 (actual) 8.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.4 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 18 (forecast) 4.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.5 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 19 (forecast) 6.4 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.5 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption on the system on Tuesday, and TransCo says the probability of interruption on Wednesday is &quot;low&quot; in every Local Distribution Zone.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
